    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is headlined today by **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), both of whom capitalize on favorable matchups against Bradish and Cole. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a +16% park adjustment and a +14% boost from his dynamic platoon splits, ensuring he remains our anchor despite facing a high-caliber arm in Cole. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned for a productive outing; the combination of a weaker opposing starter in Bradish and his aggressive placement in the #4 hole makes him an elite play. While **Heliot Ramos** (65.99) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also project as strong starts, they rely heavily on favorable park factors to offset the inherent volatility of their respective matchups, with **Sam Antonacci** notably leaning on his lead-off spot to maximize his cumulative value.\n\nOur most difficult decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who fell just shy of the starting threshold with a score of 37.99. Despite **Nasim Nunez** boasting an elite 50% stolen base holding potential\u2014a premium asset for our squad\u2014the combination of facing a dominant arm like deGrom and an unfavorable #8 spot in the order kept him below our strict floor. As we navigate the schedule, the absence of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill** continues to strain our depth, leaving us thin as we chase the scarcest categories. We remain particularly wary of the matchup for **Wade Meckler**, whose score of 48.71 is buoyed largely by his lead-off placement; any shift in the lineup order before first pitch could trigger an immediate re-evaluation of his viability as a starter.",
